# Quantum Information Hidden in Cycles

Move from local graph counts to global logical information. Start with the exact family-level explorer.

{{interactive_demo:0}}

## The conservation law

A CSS chain complex allocates the middle-space dimension among logical classes and two independent boundary ranks.

{{algorithm:0}}

<details><summary>Reveal the dimension argument</summary>Since boundaries lie among cycles, quotient dimension gives $k+\operatorname{rank}d_2=\dim\ker d_1$. Rank–nullity gives $\dim\ker d_1+\operatorname{rank}d_1=\dim B$. Eliminating the cycle dimension yields $k+\operatorname{rank}d_1+\operatorname{rank}d_2=\dim B$.</details>

For background, see [quantum error correction](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quantum_error_correction) and [homology](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homology_(mathematics)).

## Graphs turn homology into circuit rank

{{interactive_demo:1}}

{{demo:0}}

<details><summary>Why connected graphs contribute the $+1$</summary>A connected graph has a spanning tree with $V-1$ edges. Every additional edge closes one independent fundamental cycle, so $k=E-(V-1)=E-V+1$.</details>

## The hypercube verdict

{{visualization:2}}

{{algorithm:1}}

{{demo:1}}

The requested cases encode $17$, $129$, and $769$ logical qubits, not one. Explore the growth curve next.

{{visualization:0}}

## Distance requires care

{{interactive_demo:2}}

{{visualization:1}}

{{algorithm:2}}

{{demo:2}}

<details><summary>Reveal the girth proof and the distance caveat</summary>Coordinate-sum parity flips across every edge, so every closed walk has even length and triangles are impossible. Flipping two distinct coordinates in alternating order constructs a square, proving girth four. This establishes the primal graph systole; full CSS distance also requires the minimum nontrivial dual cohomology weight.</details>

Learn more about [hypercube graphs](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hypercube_graph), [cycle spaces](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cycle_space), and [CSS codes](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CSS_code).

